      "listing": {
        "summary": "YouTube on the big screen: trending, categories, search, channels, playlists, and your subscriptions with a linked Google account.",
        "description": "Browses YouTube with the YouTube Data API (v3), with an API key the server's admin creates in the Google Cloud console, and plays videos in YouTube's own IFrame player (youtube-nocookie.com) driven by Playpex's controls and remote. Adverts YouTube shows play as they would on YouTube; YouTube chooses the quality.\n\nSet up on the dashboard (Plugins › YouTube › Settings): the API key, the region of the trending rows, and what kids profiles get. To see subscriptions, liked videos and playlists, create an OAuth client of type \"TVs and Limited Input devices\" in the same Google Cloud project, enter its client id and secret, then link each profile's Google account on the Accounts tab: the person enters the code shown at google.com/device on their phone. Playpex asks for read-only access (youtube.readonly); the tokens stay on the server, encrypted, and unlinking revokes them at Google.",
